\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Triple Equivalence Validation (Theorem~2.5). (a)~Entropy $S / k_{\mathrm  {B}}$ vs.\ partition depth $\mathcal  {M}$ on log--log axes for three independent derivations: oscillation entropy $S_{\mathrm  {osc}}$, categorical entropy $S_{\mathrm  {cat}}$, and partition entropy $S_{\mathrm  {part}}$; all three produce identical values $S = k_{\mathrm  {B}}\mathcal  {M}\ln 2$ across four decades ($\mathcal  {M}= 2$ to $1000$), with the three lines perfectly overlapping. (b)~Deviation $|S_{\mathrm  {osc}} / S_{\mathrm  {cat}} - 1|$ vs.\ $\mathcal  {M}$; all residuals sit at IEEE~754 double-precision floor ($2.22 \times 10^{-16}$), confirming exact algebraic identity rather than mere numerical agreement. (c)~Three-dimensional scatter of $(\mathcal  {M},\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em} \text  {base index},\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em} S/(k_{\mathrm  {B}}\mathcal  {M}))$ for four encoding bases $b \in \{2, 3, 10, e\}$; each base produces a flat plane at height $\ln b$, confirming the general relation $S = k_{\mathrm  {B}}\mathcal  {M}\ln b$ with no cross-terms. (d)~Normalised entropy per partition operation $S / (k_{\mathrm  {B}}\mathcal  {M})$ for each base: $\ln 2 = 0.693$, $\ln 3 = 1.099$, $\ln 10 = 2.303$, $\ln e = 1.000$; the values match analytic predictions to machine precision, establishing that the triple equivalence (Oscillation $\equiv $ Category $\equiv $ Partition) holds universally regardless of encoding base.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:panel_exp4_purpose}{{1}{4}{Triple Equivalence Validation (Theorem~2.5). (a)~Entropy $S / \kB $ vs.\ partition depth $\Depth $ on log--log axes for three independent derivations: oscillation entropy $S_{\mathrm {osc}}$, categorical entropy $S_{\mathrm {cat}}$, and partition entropy $S_{\mathrm {part}}$; all three produce identical values $S = \kB \Depth \ln 2$ across four decades ($\Depth = 2$ to $1000$), with the three lines perfectly overlapping. (b)~Deviation $|S_{\mathrm {osc}} / S_{\mathrm {cat}} - 1|$ vs.\^^M$\Depth $; all residuals sit at IEEE~754 double-precision floor ($2.22 \times 10^{-16}$), confirming exact algebraic identity rather than mere numerical agreement. (c)~Three-dimensional scatter of $(\Depth ,\; \text {base index},\; S/(\kB \Depth ))$ for four encoding bases $b \in \{2, 3, 10, e\}$; each base produces a flat plane at height $\ln b$, confirming the general relation $S = \kB \Depth \ln b$ with no cross-terms. (d)~Normalised entropy per partition operation $S / (\kB \Depth )$ for each base: $\ln 2 = 0.693$, $\ln 3 = 1.099$, $\ln 10 = 2.303$, $\ln e = 1.000$; the values match analytic predictions to machine precision, establishing that the triple equivalence (Oscillation $\equiv $ Category $\equiv $ Partition) holds universally regardless of encoding base}{figure.1}{}}
