\newlabel{tab:comparison}{{3}{17}{Comparison of whole-cell modeling approaches. The Purpose instantiation framework differs fundamentally from simulation-based methods in its epistemic stance (completion rather than propagation), its treatment of uncertainty (fuzzy rather than point estimates), and its disease detection capability (trajectory escape rather than threshold comparison)}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Four-Stage Compilation Pipeline Validation (Theorems~5--7). (a)~Mean absolute relative error (MARE) at each pipeline stage on a logarithmic scale, demonstrating strict monotonic decrease: Observe ($2.67$) $\to $ Catalyze ($0.94$) $\to $ Fuse ($0.23$) $\to $ Access ($6.7 \times 10^{-11}$). The Access stage achieves machine-precision recovery of all 7 unobserved species from only 3 observations, confirming that Kirchhoff constraint completion is informationally sufficient. (b)~Completed vs.\ true concentrations for the 8 unobserved glycolytic intermediates after the Access stage; all points lie on the identity line ($y = x$, grey) with MARE $< 10^{-10}$, spanning two orders of magnitude in concentration from BPG ($0.001\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM}$) to 3PG ($0.12\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM}$). (c)~Three-dimensional view of (species index, true concentration, completed concentration) confirming pointwise agreement across the full metabolite vector without systematic bias. (d)~Grouped bars comparing three state estimates for each unobserved species: uninformative prior ($0.1\tmspace  +\thickmuskip {.2777em}\mathrm  {mM}$, grey), fused estimate after multi-modal integration (teal), and final Access result (green). The prior deviates by up to $99\times $ (BPG); fusion narrows this to ${\sim }20\%$; Access eliminates residual error entirely. Monotonic improvement held in $100\%$ of 50 Monte Carlo trials with $5\%$ observation noise.}}{17}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:panel_exp3_purpose}{{6}{17}{Four-Stage Compilation Pipeline Validation (Theorems~5--7). (a)~Mean absolute relative error (MARE) at each pipeline stage on a logarithmic scale, demonstrating strict monotonic decrease: Observe ($2.67$) $\to $ Catalyze ($0.94$) $\to $ Fuse ($0.23$) $\to $ Access ($6.7 \times 10^{-11}$). The Access stage achieves machine-precision recovery of all 7 unobserved species from only 3 observations, confirming that Kirchhoff constraint completion is informationally sufficient. (b)~Completed vs.\ true concentrations for the 8 unobserved glycolytic intermediates after the Access stage; all points lie on the identity line ($y = x$, grey) with MARE $< 10^{-10}$, spanning two orders of magnitude in concentration from BPG ($0.001\;\mathrm {mM}$) to 3PG ($0.12\;\mathrm {mM}$). (c)~Three-dimensional view of (species index, true concentration, completed concentration) confirming pointwise agreement across the full metabolite vector without systematic bias. (d)~Grouped bars comparing three state estimates for each unobserved species: uninformative prior ($0.1\;\mathrm {mM}$, grey), fused estimate after multi-modal integration (teal), and final Access result (green). The prior deviates by up to $99\times $ (BPG); fusion narrows this to ${\sim }20\%$; Access eliminates residual error entirely. Monotonic improvement held in $100\%$ of 50 Monte Carlo trials with $5\%$ observation noise}{figure.6}{}}
